# What are Packets and Frames


## Goal
    Understand better the notion of Packets and Frames

## Summary
    Packets are a piece of data from Layer 3 of the OSI Model (Network Layer), containing informations such as IP addresses and payload.
    Frames are used in Layer 2 of the OSI Model (Data Link), which encapsulates the packet and add information such as MAC addresses.

    It's similar to mailing a letter, the Frame being the envelope and the Packet the letter. 
    "Once the recepient opens the envelop (Frame), they will know how to forward the letter (Packet) itself."

    Packets have different structures depending of the type of packet sent. 
    A packet using this protocol will have a set of headers that contain additional pieces of information to the data 
    that is being sent across a network.
